.TH wc 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
wc \- print newline, word, and byte counts for each file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY wc
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SY wc
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.BI \-\-files0\-from= F
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Print newline, word, and byte counts for each FILE, and a total line if
more than one FILE is specified.  A word is a nonempty sequence of non white
space delimited by white space characters or by start or end of input.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
The options below may be used to select which counts are printed, always in
the following order: newline, word, character, byte, maximum line length.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#wc-c
\fB\-c, \-\-bytes\fP
.UE
print the byte counts
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#wc-m
\fB\-m, \-\-chars\fP
.UE
print the character counts
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#wc-l
\fB\-l, \-\-lines\fP
.UE
print the newline counts
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#wc--debug
\fB\-\-debug\fP
.UE
indicate what line count acceleration is used
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#wc--files0-from
\fB\-\-files0\-from=F\fP
.UE
read input from the files specified by
NUL\-terminated names in file F;
If F is \-, read names from standard input
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#wc-L
\fB\-L, \-\-max\-line\-length\fP
.UE
print the maximum display width
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#wc-w
\fB\-w, \-\-words\fP
.UE
print the word counts
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#wc--total
\fB\-\-total=WHEN\fP
.UE
when to print a line with total counts;
WHEN can be: auto, always, only, never
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/wc#wc--help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/wc#wc--version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
